<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Proholding halted for OPA.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Proholding halted for OPA.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in chemical holding Proholding SGPS was suspended earlier today by the Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) following the preliminary announcement of a public offer to buy (OPA) for the concern, a committee official told Reuters.</p>
<p>He declined to give further details.</p>
<p>The major shareholder in Proholding is Imparfim-Investimentos &amp; Participacoes Financeiras, a holding company belonging to the family of Belmiro de Azevedo, chairman of the Sonae group, market sources said.</p>
<p>Proholding is not part of the Sonae group.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
